                <pb facs="0295" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860d.01/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-22T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 22,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.57
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>868. Your 792, February 19, 4 p.m. The following telegram has been sent to the
                    Legation at Stockholm: <pb facs="0296" n="211" xml:id="pg211"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your 100, February 15, 6 p.m. Please say to Minister Enckell that I am
                            unable to answer his question as the matter is still under consideration
                            but that I shall not fail to advise you as soon as a decision has been
                            reached. Copy of this telegram has been sent to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed>Lansing</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
